lines+=['', 'All 31,457,280 immutable selections are counted once; the tied head/embedding is counted once. K64 book allocation reserves 491,520 domains × 16 UINT8 slots = 7,864,320 B, a derived padded capacity. October reports 7,765,892 used representative bytes; padding is not new model content. Native per-projection coefficient ROM formats are replaced by selections/books, not added as SRAM. Native metadata totals are 368,640 readmem metadata B + 61,440 producer/norm case-ROM B + 5,270.5 small case-ROM B = 435,350.5 B. Frontend coefficients remain 8,298,240 B of FP32 binary ROM. Other native coefficient bytes are not added again.','', 'Inventory source reports 28,641,280 newly on-chip ROM B plus 8,852,630.5 already-on-chip case-ROM B. These describe the elaborated native representation, not an extra memory allocation on top of Taalas weights. Ordinary registers are costed separately at 63.6608 µm² per `dffq_1` cell / 0.5 utilization. This can conservatively duplicate register area already embedded in engine/control allowances; no unsupported subtraction was made.','', '### Mutable memory replaces both reserves','', '**MEASURED inventory:** 8,501,818 array bits = 1,062,727.25 B, 144 declarations / 321 instances; 237,524 ordinary register bits = 29,690.5 B. Source is Verilator elaboration of the merged all-on-chip top, 30,542 instances, not a Yosys mapped-memory result. Both old reserve blocks are removed; no ungrounded conservative reserve row remains.','', 'The [per-array allocation](memory_allocation.json) preserves each declaration instance and ceil(width/8) byte lanes, flattens array dimensions, and chooses the least-area homogeneous depth banking among the real 64/128/256/512×8 LEFs. This yields **2,892 macros**, **1,210,112 allocated bytes**, **539.853 mm²** of measured LEF rectangles and **593.838 mm²** after an assumed 10% internal placement allowance. Single-port compatibility, simultaneous accesses, bank muxes and RTL replacement are not proven. Small arrays can be inefficient in these macros; no free cross-array packing was assumed.','', 'Research memory uses 0.9479839488 mm² per 4,096 B, independently capacity-rounded per instance: 553.717 mm² with the same 10% allowance. The small research/open difference comes from many small instances wasting large banks; it is not a contradiction in bit density. Dense custom uses an assumed effective 12 µm²/bit plus 10% group placement allowance: 112.224 mm². Its effective density already includes cell periphery, and requires a compiled/characterized macro.','', '### Bank-height and engine evidence','', '| Bank rows | Measured partial assembly µm²/selection | Whole-model partial array mm² | Timing qualification |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
