lines+=['', f"`stdcell`: (8.255466688−6.137030637) mm²/409,600 = **{cfg['scenarios']['stdcell']['selection_um2']:.6f} µm²/selection** synthesized-cell differential, then /0.5 utilization. This paired-run difference is measured synthesis evidence, not an isolated selection macro or routed density. Mapping changes can affect the subtraction. `custom7` uses7.04×1.25; `optimistic3_5` uses3.5×1.25, both assumptions. Measured64/320/1280 use actual partial bounding boxes without another blanket periphery multiplier. Binary ROM uses the explicit1.76 µm²/bit×1.25 assumption.", '', 'Levers on: frontend coefficients FP32→INT8 (2,074,560 B), books stored at selection density/4 per bit, and the actual compact self-attention `keys`/`values` arrays FP32→8-bit (168,960 B→42,240 B). Only those two measured KV arrays receive KV8 savings; committed history and arbitrary state do not. Frontend INT8 and KV8 **require model-accuracy re-validation**. Books-in-array retains numeric values but needs new read/access hardware. With today’s wide measured readout layout it increases book area, so the combined “on” case can be larger. No assumed accuracy or timing benefit is credited.','', '### Power and IO scope','', 'Core voltage is3.3 V, matching `gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__tt_025C_3v30`. All listed watts are **ASSUMED**. W5 explicitly leaves full320-lane read energy null; its new selected16-active-column group includes128receiver channels and partial WL/PC drivers. At40ns the measured partial source sums are51.344pJ TT and41.439pJ SS, including finite-window charge-return effects; they are not full-row energies. Scaling that number to full-row energy would misrepresent the evidence. W2b workload power remains unannotated; its7.32749 W default/propagated estimate is recorded as an unqualified comparator and not silently used as speech power. Consequently this IR screen proves neither sub-watt operation nor worst-workload voltage margin.','', 'Supply-pad pairs = ceil(2×P/(3.3 V×25 mA)), rounded up to a multiple of four; die B increases the16pair current-derived minimum to32pairs for IR.25 mA and2× current margin are assumptions. Actual GF180 `dvdd`, `dvss`, `bi_t`, corner and filler LEFs form abutting rings. Supply feeds use Metal2 to the Metal4/5 core ring; macro vertical Metal4 pins connect to the horizontal Metal5 grid. Core rings40 µm, straps400 µm pitch; all selected straps40 µm. Per-macro static current derives from its assigned power /3.3 V. Voltage sources are at transformed supply-pad terminals.','', 'The technology LEF sheet/via resistances are screening values (Metal4 .09 Ω/square, Metal5 .06 Ω/square), not qualified extraction. Package/bond resistance, transient droop, EM and macro-internal resistance are absent. Supply connectivity is implemented; IO signal nets, configuration/tie controls, clock and recognizer signal routes are not. The artifact therefore has a connected **abstract supply pad ring**, not a demonstrated functional pad interface.','', '### Reproduction and provenance','', '[Input refresh audit](input_refresh_audit.json) verifies that newly snapshotted progress/timing updates do not change the actual areas, loads or engine footprint in the completed runs. See [MEASURED_COMMANDS.md](MEASURED_COMMANDS.md), [source hashes](results.json), [per-array allocation](memory_allocation.json), [blocks.json](blocks.json) and [machine results](results.json). All writes and active outputs remain inside this workspace. EDA runs use nice10, at most4threads, sequential execution, a22GiB free-space guard and600s/run guard. Original failures are retained. The earlier assumption-based report is preserved as [historical report](historical_pre_measured_RESULTS.md) and is superseded by this section.','']
